{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>טוב</b>, <b>לא</b> — two joined words." "<b>יָפִיק</b> — meaning 'he will bring out,' that is, a good man will bring out the will of HaShem, that is, He will accept him." "<b>וְאִישׁ מְזִמּוֹת</b> — evil thoughts, HaShem will condemn when He judges; therefore [the verse comes] after it."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra notes that these two words from the verse are syntactically bound together; the note is extremely terse and the exact grammatical point he is making is not elaborated.", 2 "The phrase 'אחריו' (after it) likely refers to the logical sequence of the verse's two halves; rendered hyper-literally as the Hebrew is terse and possibly compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:21.515985395Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}